The Rat Who Smiles.


18 Nov 2020 00:20








I moved and trimmed your thread summary, since it was taking up extra space in the main forum screen. Try to keep thread descriptions (the text in the little box under the thread title) and titles short so you don't crowd out other authors in the forum listing. ~Zyn

Seeking Greenlights:  Yes

Page Type:  SCP Article

Elevator Pitch: 

This SCP is a pitch black humanoid like creature with a head of that of a cartoony rat. It doesn't do anything however it just watches however he affects his victim with strange dreams and visions. It has only recently been designated as an SCP but it has been seemingly affecting people for decades and now it seems to be affecting adults now.

Central Narrative: 

As the Rat gets designated as an SCP the foundation prepares to conduct multiple interviews with the staff that were affected by the Rat. The staff then describe the dreams and visions the rat would give them as they also describe how every dream would end with it watching them smiling as they would wake up. At first that was the extent of it but recently multiple staff have reported seeing it again.

+block

–block


Hook/Attention-Grabber: 

In this SCP Article I will be compiling many of the strange dreams I've had in the past as well as some things I may just make up. This includes being stuck on a high chair as the octopus from the wiggles approaches you, Being trapped in a car with an ape of some sort being outside the door trying to get in violently and so on. Also I hope to add some backstory with some dreams.

Additional Notes: 

This will be a combination of many of the very strange dreams I've had in the past and yes I used to be scared of a tall pitch black rat man when I was a kid.

I will try to recreate a child-like drawing of the rat for the article's picture. Going to add a narrative to the story as many of the reoccurring dreams will be related to the rats past. Interviews will be used to add character.





